                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Yes I'm target gray-bearded money-bag audience who's been loading King's Bounty from floppy.\nNo I don't like RPG MO.\n\n(+) Really open world. Some places are blocked by hi-level mobs or some keys, its normal. Well, King's Bounty in 1988 was open-world, too. Good things hadn't changed in 40 years (really?).\n(+) Really chilling gameplay. Yes reminders about events and donation drop regularly, but they're only in chat, not annoying. If you don't move your mouse, nothing happens.\n(+) 200-300 players online. Even my noob offers on market were redeemed.\n\n(-) Etherything's intentionally sloooow. You strike a mob and time ticks. Mob strikes back and time ticks. You swing a pickaxe and time ticks. You miss a stone (yes! a serious chance to miss a stone!) and wait for next swing. I had to play another game while playing this game...\n(-) Grind is grindy grind. I'm not much a player in modern MMOs, but seems RPGMO is in grindtop grindtier. Routine hourly quest is say collecting 500 wood. Each wood is 3 seconds. 5x500/60=25 minutes. Speedrun of King's Bounty (yes there are some :) is 21 minutes. That guy had earned all glory of the world, while I was cutting 1 tree.\n(-) You cannot leave the game play itself. There's captcha with randomized interval +-10 minutes! And penalty for not performing!\n(-) Inventory is intentionally small and items don't stack! Now I have 40 slots. To deliver 500 wood from previous quest, I have to perform 500/40=13 journeys from forest to town chest. Back and forth. Back and forth. To have 48 slots, everybody take off all gear and go farming with axe in hand and with no pants.\n(-/+) Yes there is affordable private island. Exactly it's totally private. There's totally no way to visit other player's islands. Just beg for screenshots. It's limited 13x13 tiles - not too small, but just 1 screen. 1 veggy bed is made from 35 water bottles (??). To make bottles, I had to roam wilderness digging about 150 sand. One veggy bed. While that guy from KB conquests castle after castle.\n(-) 1 wall is made of 100 wood. Walls are pure decoration. No one visits your island, remember?\n(-) Seeds don't reproduce. One single way to get seeds is buying from NPC.\n(-) 11 years in early access. Ingame sales are enough for devs' sausage & beer. Please let me not see what will occur on release.\n\nMuch more like a tabletop party for few devoted friends, than a MMO.\n\nThis game has done no evil to me. Nobody was cheating me. I've spent no money. I had some fun. I stopped playing as soon as my astonishment turned into anxiety. RPGMO is on the light side. For that weak reason I'm not abusing their effort with negative appraisal.",
